=== (0) THE EIGHT RELEASES — what each SHIPS, parsed and not assumed (HARD RULE 1) ===
  brfss            3 files ·   2.50 GB · {'.zip': 1, '.xpt': 1, '.xpt ': 1}
  dataverse       34 files ·   0.03 GB · {'.do': 8, '.dta': 8, '.sav': 8, '.zip': 5, '.xls': 2}
  dplace         574 files ·   0.87 GB · {'.csv': 222, '.trees': 208, '': 41, '.gz': 19, '.xlsx': 17}
  gss              8 files ·   0.65 GB · {'.pdf': 4, '.zip': 1, '.log': 1, '.txt': 1, '.dta': 1}
  ngram            3 files ·   0.00 GB · {'.json': 1, '.py': 1, '.log': 1}
  nsfg            19 files ·   0.57 GB · {'.dat': 15, '.dct': 3, '.sas': 1}
  openpsych       28 files ·   0.05 GB · {'.csv': 10, '.txt': 9, '.zip': 8, '.html': 1}
  yrbs            11 files ·   1.65 GB · {'.dat': 8, '.sas': 2, '.zip': 1}

=== (1) THE SUPPORT MATRIX — 8 releases × 3 estimands, every cell reported ===

  brfss
     UNREADABLE     (1) comonotonicity: >=3 series x >=8 waves
     NOT SUPPORTED  (2) case-indexed norm x sanction, >=2 cases both sides
     UNREADABLE     (3) person-level norm vs a second measured quantity
     why: 1 `.XPT` and NO codebook in the directory (`#891`) ⇒ terse names only

  dataverse
     NOT SUPPORTED  (1) comonotonicity: >=3 series x >=8 waves
     NOT SUPPORTED  (2) case-indexed norm x sanction, >=2 cases both sides
     SUPPORTED      (3) person-level norm vs a second measured quantity
     why: replication packages: single-study `.dta`, no wave structure

  dplace
     NOT SUPPORTED  (1) comonotonicity: >=3 series x >=8 waves
     NOT SUPPORTED  (2) case-indexed norm x sanction, >=2 cases both sides
     SUPPORTED      (3) person-level norm vs a second measured quantity
     why: one observation per society ⇒ no waves at all (`#897` measured that its crossed design cannot resolve ANY effect); societies are the unit for (3)

  gss
     SUPPORTED      (1) comonotonicity: >=3 series x >=8 waves
     SUPPORTED      (2) case-indexed norm x sanction, >=2 cases both sides
     SUPPORTED      (3) person-level norm vs a second measured quantity
     why: 6943 labelled variables · 34 waves · the only release shipping question text

  ngram
     NOT SUPPORTED  (1) comonotonicity: >=3 series x >=8 waves
     NOT SUPPORTED  (2) case-indexed norm x sanction, >=2 cases both sides
     NOT SUPPORTED  (3) person-level norm vs a second measured quantity
     why: a curves JSON of word frequencies; no respondents, no items, no norms

  nsfg
     NOT SUPPORTED  (1) comonotonicity: >=3 series x >=8 waves
     NOT SUPPORTED  (2) case-indexed norm x sanction, >=2 cases both sides
     UNREADABLE     (3) person-level norm vs a second measured quantity
     why: 15 data files but only 4 shipped layouts ⇒ 2 readable cycles; the IH attitude block is **4 items**, of which 2 are norms — too few for (1) and no sanction side for (2)

  openpsych
     NOT SUPPORTED  (1) comonotonicity: >=3 series x >=8 waves
     NOT SUPPORTED  (2) case-indexed norm x sanction, >=2 cases both sides
     SUPPORTED      (3) person-level norm vs a second measured quantity
     why: cross-sectional scale releases: no waves ⇒ (1) impossible; no sanction side ⇒ (2) impossible; person-level item data ⇒ (3) available

  yrbs
     UNREADABLE     (1) comonotonicity: >=3 series x >=8 waves
     NOT SUPPORTED  (2) case-indexed norm x sanction, >=2 cases both sides
     UNREADABLE     (3) person-level norm vs a second measured quantity
     why: the NATIONAL file ships only as an Access `.MDB` inside a zip; the readable `.dat` files are district/state. Behaviour items, no norm×sanction pair

